{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Knot.WhiteheadSaddleClausen","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Knot.WhiteheadSaddleClausen","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Knot.Clausen","lean:module:QOU.Knot.WhiteheadVolumeConjecture"],"declarations":31,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.WhiteheadSaddle.whitehead_vc_innerSum_half","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.WhiteheadSaddle.whitehead_vc_innerSum_half","kind":"theorem","line":721,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/WhiteheadSaddleClausen.lean#L721-L811","doc":"**The Whitehead Volume Conjecture for the `⌊N/2⌋`-level inner sum**\n(UNCONDITIONAL, sorry-free): `(2π/N)·log(Σ_k S_{⌊N/2⌋,k}) → 4·catalanG = 4G`.\n\nSqueeze: below by the explicit `k*=⌊N/4⌋` saddle term\n(`whiteheadS_explicit_saddle_tendsto`, BRICK 3), above by the\n`k`-independent envelope `(2π/N)·log N + whiteheadUmax N` (max-term\n`≤ whiteheadUmax N` for every `k` incl. `k=0` via\n`two_pi_log_whiteheadS_le_all`, slack `(2π/N)·log N → 0`), both `→ 4·G`.\nThis closes the analytic limit left open in\n`QOU.Knot.WhiteheadVC.whitehead_volume_conjecture` (bean qou-1gkf). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.WhiteheadSaddle.whiteheadS_explicit_saddle_tendsto","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.WhiteheadSaddle.whiteheadS_explicit_saddle_tendsto","kind":"theorem","line":681,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/WhiteheadSaddleClausen.lean#L681-L719","doc":"**Explicit saddle-term convergence (BRICK 3).**  At the saddle\n`(n*, k*) = (⌊N/2⌋, ⌊N/4⌋)`, `(2π/N)·log S_{n*,k*} → 4·catalanG = 4G`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.WhiteheadSaddle.two_pi_log_whiteheadS_le_all","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.WhiteheadSaddle.two_pi_log_whiteheadS_le_all","kind":"theorem","line":639,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/WhiteheadSaddleClausen.lean#L639-L679","doc":"**Uniform per-term upper bound over the WHOLE range** `0 ≤ k ≤ N-1-⌊N/2⌋`\n(BRICK 5a extended to the `k = 0` maximizer edge via `clausen_nonneg`):\nevery term satisfies `(2π/N)·log S_{⌊N/2⌋,k} ≤ whiteheadUmax N`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.WhiteheadSaddle.whiteheadUmax","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.WhiteheadSaddle.whiteheadUmax","kind":"def","line":632,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/WhiteheadSaddleClausen.lean#L632-L637","doc":"The `k`-independent upper envelope from BRICK 5a, packaged as a named\nsequence.  Its limit is `4·catalanG = 4G` (grid points `⌊N/2⌋π/N → π/2`,\n`2⌊N/2⌋π/N → π`; `devErr → 0`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.WhiteheadSaddle.devErr_nonneg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.WhiteheadSaddle.devErr_nonneg","kind":"theorem","line":619,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/WhiteheadSaddleClausen.lean#L619-L630","doc":"`devErr N ≥ 0` — every summand of the master error is nonnegative. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.WhiteheadSaddle.two_pi_log_whiteheadS_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.WhiteheadSaddle.two_pi_log_whiteheadS_le","kind":"theorem","line":579,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/WhiteheadSaddleClausen.lean#L579-L617","doc":"**Uniform per-term upper bound (BRICK 5a).**  For every valid `k`,\n`(2π/N)·log S_{⌊N/2⌋,k} ≤ 4·clausen(π − ⌊N/2⌋π/N) + clausen(2⌊N/2⌋π/N) +\n10·devErr N` — a `k`-independent RHS (the parity-clean upper envelope via\n`clausen_diff_le_shift` at `s = 2⌊N/2⌋π/N`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.WhiteheadSaddle.clausen_nonneg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.WhiteheadSaddle.clausen_nonneg","kind":"theorem","line":538,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/WhiteheadSaddleClausen.lean#L538-L577","doc":"`clausen ≥ 0` on `[0,π]` (the positive lobe): `clausen(0)=clausen(π)=0`,\nincreasing to the max at `π/3`, then decreasing. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.WhiteheadSaddle.gridPrim_ge","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.WhiteheadSaddle.gridPrim_ge","kind":"theorem","line":532,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/WhiteheadSaddleClausen.lean#L532-L536","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.WhiteheadSaddle.gridPrim_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.WhiteheadSaddle.gridPrim_le","kind":"theorem","line":526,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/WhiteheadSaddleClausen.lean#L526-L530","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.WhiteheadSaddle.tendsto_devErr","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.WhiteheadSaddle.tendsto_devErr","kind":"theorem","line":523,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/WhiteheadSaddleClausen.lean#L523-L524","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.WhiteheadSaddle.devErr","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.WhiteheadSaddle.devErr","kind":"def","line":518,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/WhiteheadSaddleClausen.lean#L518-L521","doc":"The `abs_deviation_le` master error as a named sequence (= `tendsto_master_error`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.WhiteheadSaddle.clausen_diff_le_shift","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.WhiteheadSaddle.clausen_diff_le_shift","kind":"theorem","line":448,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/WhiteheadSaddleClausen.lean#L448-L516","doc":"**Generalized global bound.** `clausen θ − clausen(θ+s) ≤ 2·clausen(π−s/2)`\n(peak at `θ = π−s/2`, value `2·clausen(π−s/2)` via `clausen(π+s/2) =\n−clausen(π−s/2)`), for `0 < s ≤ π`, `0 ≤ θ ≤ 2π−s`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.WhiteheadSaddle.hasDerivAt_clausen_diff_shift","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.WhiteheadSaddle.hasDerivAt_clausen_diff_shift","kind":"theorem","line":436,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/WhiteheadSaddleClausen.lean#L436-L446","doc":"Derivative of the shifted-Clausen difference for a general shift `s` on the\ninterior of its domain. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.WhiteheadSaddle.clausen_diff_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.WhiteheadSaddle.clausen_diff_le","kind":"theorem","line":380,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/WhiteheadSaddleClausen.lean#L380-L434","doc":"**Upper-envelope global bound (BRICK 4a).**  `clausen θ − clausen(θ+π) ≤\n2·clausen(π/2)` on `[0,π]` — the shifted-integrand max at the saddle\n`θ = π/2` (E2/E3 analogue). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.WhiteheadSaddle.hasDerivAt_clausen_diff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.WhiteheadSaddle.hasDerivAt_clausen_diff","kind":"theorem","line":368,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/WhiteheadSaddleClausen.lean#L368-L378","doc":"Derivative of the van der Veen shifted-Clausen difference on `(0,π)`:\n`d/dθ [clausen θ − clausen(θ+π)] = log(2 sin((θ+π)/2)) − log(2 sin(θ/2))`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.WhiteheadSaddle.gridpt_tendsto","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.WhiteheadSaddle.gridpt_tendsto","kind":"theorem","line":330,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/WhiteheadSaddleClausen.lean#L330-L366","doc":"Grid-point limit helper: integer bounds `a·N − c ≤ b·Kseq ≤ a·N` (b>0) give\n`2·Kseq·(π/N) → 2(a/b)π`.  (The figure-eight (b) squeeze, parameterized.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.WhiteheadSaddle.gridPrim_tendsto","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.WhiteheadSaddle.gridPrim_tendsto","kind":"theorem","line":304,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/WhiteheadSaddleClausen.lean#L304-L328","doc":"**gridPrim limit brick (BRICK 2).**  At a moving index `Kseq N` with\n`2·Kseq·(π/N) → θ` and `1 ≤ Kseq ≤ N−1` (eventually), `S'(Kseq) → −clausen(θ)/2`\n— `abs_deviation_le` squeeze + `continuous_clausen` (figure-eight (b)+(c)). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.WhiteheadSaddle.two_pi_log_whiteheadS_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.WhiteheadSaddle.two_pi_log_whiteheadS_eq","kind":"theorem","line":265,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/WhiteheadSaddleClausen.lean#L265-L302","doc":"**Regroup brick (BRICK 1).** `(2π/N)·log S_{n,k} = 4·S'(k+n) − 4·S'(k) − 2·S'(n)`\n(the log2-fold of `whiteheadS_log`, then `gridPrim_shift`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.WhiteheadSaddle.whiteheadS_sin_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.WhiteheadSaddle.whiteheadS_sin_pos","kind":"theorem","line":239,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/WhiteheadSaddleClausen.lean#L239-L263","doc":"Both van der Veen sines are positive on the summation range (the two facts\ninside `whiteheadS_factor_pos`, in the `(π/N)`-argument form). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.WhiteheadSaddle.gridPrim_shift","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.WhiteheadSaddle.gridPrim_shift","kind":"theorem","line":214,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/WhiteheadSaddleClausen.lean#L214-L237","doc":"**Reindex/telescope brick.** The shifted grid sum equals a gridPrim\ndifference: `(π/N)·Σ_{j=1}^n log(2 sin((k+j)π/N)) = S'(k+n) − S'(k)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.WhiteheadSaddle.gridPrim","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.WhiteheadSaddle.gridPrim","kind":"def","line":209,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/WhiteheadSaddleClausen.lean#L209-L212","doc":"Grid Clausen-primitive `S'(N,K) = (π/N)·Σ_{j=1}^K log(2 sin(jπ/N))` — the\nobject `QOU.Knot.abs_deviation_le` bounds by `−clausen(2Kπ/N)/2`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.WhiteheadSaddle.catalanG_eq_clausen_pi_div_two","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.WhiteheadSaddle.catalanG_eq_clausen_pi_div_two","kind":"theorem","line":158,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/WhiteheadSaddleClausen.lean#L158-L205","doc":"**catalan bridge (convergence prerequisite, qou-kvvu).**  Catalan's constant\n`G = Σ (-1)ⁿ/(2n+1)²` equals `clausen(π/2)`: the even/odd split of the `Cl_2`\nseries drops the even-index (`sin(mπ)=0`) terms and reindexes the odd-index\nterms `sin((2k+1)π/2) = (-1)ᵏ`.  Connects the conditional-VC constant\n`4·catalanG` (`whitehead_vc_of_saddle_value`) to the Clausen value\n`4·clausen(π/2)` produced by `saddle_integral`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.WhiteheadSaddle.sin_odd_index_vanish","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.WhiteheadSaddle.sin_odd_index_vanish","kind":"theorem","line":149,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/WhiteheadSaddleClausen.lean#L149-L156","doc":"The odd-indexed `Cl_2`-series term (series index `j = 2k+1`) has vanishing\nsine: `sin(((2k+1)+1)·(π/2)) = sin((k+1)π) = 0`. These are the terms dropped\nby the even/odd split in `catalanG_eq_clausen_pi_div_two`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.WhiteheadSaddle.sin_two_mul_add_one_mul_pi_div_two","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.WhiteheadSaddle.sin_two_mul_add_one_mul_pi_div_two","kind":"theorem","line":136,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/WhiteheadSaddleClausen.lean#L136-L147","doc":"`sin((2k+1)·(π/2)) = (-1)^k` (induction; each step adds `π`, `sin_add_pi`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.WhiteheadSaddle.saddle_integral","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.WhiteheadSaddle.saddle_integral","kind":"theorem","line":119,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/WhiteheadSaddleClausen.lean#L119-L134","doc":"**Saddle VALUE identity (sorry-free).**  The (log2-reduced) saddle integrand\nintegrates to `2·clausen(π/2)/π`, so `2π ×` it `= 4·clausen(π/2) = 4G` — the\nvalue half of `hsaddle`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.WhiteheadSaddle.integral_A","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.WhiteheadSaddle.integral_A","kind":"theorem","line":98,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/WhiteheadSaddleClausen.lean#L98-L117","doc":"The shifted `log(2 sin(π(u+¼)))` piece: `∫_0^{1/2} = clausen(π/2)/π`\n(shift to `[¼,¾]`, split, `integral_log_two_sin_pi` at `¾,¼`, antisymmetry). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.WhiteheadSaddle.integral_B_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.WhiteheadSaddle.integral_B_zero","kind":"theorem","line":90,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/WhiteheadSaddleClausen.lean#L90-L96","doc":"The `−log(2 sin(π u))` piece: `∫_0^{1/2} log(2 sin(π u)) du = 0`\n(`= −clausen(π)/(2π)` and `clausen π = 0`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.WhiteheadSaddle.clausen_three_pi_div_two","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.WhiteheadSaddle.clausen_three_pi_div_two","kind":"theorem","line":81,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/WhiteheadSaddleClausen.lean#L81-L88","doc":"`clausen(3π/2) = −clausen(π/2)` (via the `clausen↔Cl_2` bridge + `Cl_2_two_pi_sub`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.WhiteheadSaddle.intervalIntegrable_log_two_sin_pi","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.WhiteheadSaddle.intervalIntegrable_log_two_sin_pi","kind":"theorem","line":74,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/WhiteheadSaddleClausen.lean#L74-L79","doc":"`log(2 sin(π·))` is interval-integrable (scale `QOU.Knot.intervalIntegrable_log_two_sin`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.WhiteheadSaddle.log_factor_reduce","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.WhiteheadSaddle.log_factor_reduce","kind":"theorem","line":59,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/WhiteheadSaddleClausen.lean#L59-L72","doc":"**Per-term reduction (convergence brick, qou-1gkf).**  Each van der Veen\nkernel factor `2 sin²a / sin b` has log equal to the reduced saddle-integrand\nterm `2 log(2 sin a) − log(2 sin b)` (the `log 2` bookkeeping that makes the\ndiscrete Riemann sum match `saddle_integral`).  Needs `sin a, sin b > 0`\n(holds on the summation range `(k+j)π/N, jπ/N ∈ (0, π)`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.WhiteheadSaddle.integral_log_two_sin_pi","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.WhiteheadSaddle.integral_log_two_sin_pi","kind":"theorem","line":49,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/WhiteheadSaddleClausen.lean#L49-L57","doc":"π-scaled `log(2 sin)` integral: `∫_0^b log(2 sin(π u)) du = -clausen(2πb)/(2π)`\n(substitution `w = π u` in `QOU.Knot.integral_log_two_sin`). ","signatureChunk":0}]}